    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_OverviewNativeHdrClear">No games have EnableSystemHdr on. Display Manager owns HDR.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_OverviewNativeHdrConflictFormat">{0} game(s) still have EnableSystemHdr on — NX clears it on launch so restores do not stack.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_NativeHdrMigrationTitle">Native EnableSystemHdr migration</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_NativeHdrMigrationHelp">Playnite’s “Enable HDR Support” checkbox stays visible — there is no public SDK API to hide it. Display Manager clears the flag so native and NX restores do not stack. Reversible from this page.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_NativeHdrStatusFormat">{0} game(s) still have EnableSystemHdr on · backup: {1} id(s).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_NativeHdrClearNow">Clear native HDR flags now</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_NativeHdrRestoreBackup">Restore from backup</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_NativeHdrClearedFormat">Cleared {0} game(s). Remaining with flag on: {1}.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_NativeHdrRestoredFormat">Restored {0} game(s). Games with flag on now: {1}.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_NativeHdrRestoreConfirm">Restore EnableSystemHdr=true for games in the Display Manager backup? Native and NX HDR may stack again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCDisplayManager_NativeHdrConflictNotice">Display Manager cleared Playnite’s native Enable HDR flag on a game so HDR restores do not stack. NX policy still applies.</sys:String>
